Track 2: Astrid at the Gabled Zenith
- Story & Context: During the longest storm of the solstice, astronomer Astrid Holm barricaded herself on the roof of Hammerfest’s municipal hall with an unspooling reel-to-reel deck, fighting off hypothermia by tracking the planetary transit of Saturn while her fingers split beneath wool mitts. When the building's generator sputtered, dropping the attic studio's voltage, the Roland Juno's clock warped down to thirty percent of its tempo, locking in sync with Astrid's terrified, decelerating pulse. Mats later layered his confession over that dying circuit, whispering through a frosted muffler, "You said you saw a burning moon, but you were only shivering."
