Track 3: "Did You Keep the Lens Warm?"
- Story & Context: When the regional power grid collapsed across northern Finnmark, local pirate transmitter Mount Storsteinen broadcast this sprawling, twelve-minute myth across empty marine frequencies to an estimated forty thousand citizens shivering under down comforters. The track's climax defied electronic music convention: after an eight-minute progressive build of lowpass saws and breathy vocal harmonies, every drum track vanished, leaving only the sound of a woodstove door latching shut and the lingering rhythm of a mammal stirring in warm straw. In the quiet morning after, fishermen claimed the track made the harbor feel ten degrees warmer, remembering Mats’s final, radio-cracked inquiry: "Did you keep the lens warm, or did the ice find you first?"
